"suggestion":"1) Unify the material language: Soften the HUD elements to match the scene. Replace the hard, sharp corner brackets with softer, rounded frames or a subtle vignette that blends into the background. 2) Elevate the player character: Add a rim light or a subtle glow to the net and the character's body to match the luminosity of the creatures, ensuring they read as part of the same world. 3) Fix the Control Deck visibility: Increase the contrast of the placeholder faces in the collection slots. Use a slightly lighter background for the slots or add a subtle stroke to the faces so the 'empty' state is clearly legible. 4) Refine the 'Collection' button: Reduce the intensity of the glow and align the border weight with the rest of the UI to create a more cohesive, premium feel."
}

